{
  "summary": "The investigation focuses on determining whether the instrument-air interruption originated at the source, within the distribution system (e.g., valves M-101/M-102), or at the receiving header H-R during boundary preparation for WO-527. Evidence confirms that maintenance release was pending and no temporary instruction attachment is recorded in the work package cover field, though physical presence remains unverified.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "statement": "The air interruption occurred while a two-person Utilities crew (U-A/U-B) was preparing to accept boundary for WO-527 at ~10:00 AM on May 20, 2024. RHOB operations observed the low-pressure indication.",
      "type": "finding",
      "status": "verified","sourceIds":["incident-description","36f83919-8b7a-4ec0-a789-5d3e24cdaf6f"],"testNeeded":"none"}
    ],
    "questions":[
      {
        "intent": "Determine if the interruption originated at the air source, distribution system (valves M-101/M-102), or receiving header H-R.",
        "text": "What physical evidence exists to distinguish whether the pressure loss began upstream of P-U, within the gallery/distribution between P-U and H-R, or downstream at H-R?",
        "rationale":"The incident description states that supporting records will be provided as investigation develops. The current packet does not establish origin location.",
        "evidenceNeeded": ["Pressure logs from multiple points (P-U, intermediate nodes if available), valve position records for M-101/M-102 at 09:48–10:07, or field observations of leakage/valve state.","Field photographs showing any open valves, leaks, or abnormal conditions in the gallery between preparation start and interruption."],
        "priority": "high",
        "sourceIds":["incident-description","aa0527b9-a6e3-4782-bb4e-b6cc9eb9dbcc"],"routedTo":[],"causalBranch":"origin-location"}
      ],
      "handoffs": [],"decision": {
        "summary": "The investigation has identified the event and confirmed that maintenance release was pending. The origin of the interruption remains unknown, requiring further evidence to separate source failure from distribution or receiving equipment issues.",
        "evidenceUsed":["incident-description","36f83919-8b7a-4ec0-a789-5d3e24cdaf6f","aa0527b9-a6e3-4782-bb4e-b6cc9eb9dbcc"],"unknowns":["Origin of interruption (source vs. distribution vs. receiving)","Valve states during boundary preparation","Whether a temporary instruction was physically attached despite blank field on cover copy"],
        "alternatives": ["Interruption caused by upstream source failure.","Interruption caused by valve M-101/M-102 being open or leaking due to setup error.","Interruption caused at receiving header H-R (e.g., internal blockage, control malfunction).","Temporary instruction was physically attached but not recorded in the cover field."],
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    }
